Presidential elections were held in [[Moldova]] on 8 December 1991.<ref name="NS">[[Dieter Nohlen]] & Philip Stöver (2010) ''Elections in Europe: A data handbook'', p1330 {{ISBN|978-3-8329-5609-7}}</ref> Due to a boycott by the [[Popular Front of Moldova]], incumbent [[Mircea Snegur]] was the only candidate to contest the elections and was elected unopposed.<ref>Nohlen & Stöver, p1343</ref>

==Background==
The elections were held amid high ethnic tensions, with separatists in [[Gagauzia]] and [[Transnistria]] declaring they would not participate in the elections.

